6 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078391 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186432241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078391 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186432242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078391 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle by Completing the Square with Fractions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078391 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186078248 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078391 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "98e3f3b4-8dfa-515c-90b1-09fb19d68144" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078682 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078682 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078682 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078682 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078682 #edb/ref 1045 "Determining Circle Properties by Completing the Square" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078682 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186079239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078682 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078682 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078682 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f525d904-1978-5a65-97fe-fc43e27af14e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079203 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186077996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079203 #edb/ref 1069 "q-76089" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079203 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079203 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n${x}^{2}+5x+{y}^{2}-2y=\\frac{7}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079203 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7f67332a-d49b-5dc7-b92a-6be6456a8b20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079203 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5x+{y}^{2}-2y & =\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+5x)+({y}^{2}-2y) & =\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}x+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 1y+{1}^{2}) & =\\frac{7}{4}+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+{1}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}x+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 1y+{1}^{2}) & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ {(x-(-\\frac{5}{2}))}^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={3}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-\\frac{5}{2},1)$ and its radius is $3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079239 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079239 #edb/ref 1061 10942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079239 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5a84eb88-0914-5665-a28e-3f5d962dbbb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079239 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186079635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079240 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079240 #edb/ref 1061 10943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079240 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "da3fbfb0-744f-5f91-919e-01f09b8883ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079240 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079241 #edb/ref 1061 10944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079241 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b6b51693-4400-5067-a52d-d029374ca40a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079241 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079635 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the equation \n\n$$\nx^2 +  y^2 - 2x - 4y = 4.\n$$\n\nBelieve it or not, this equation actually represents a circle! Its graph is given below:\n\n![](images/5d/5dfea5042d6c84f40a2790a01ee6aafb64433f7422ce88b589cf670d93771e2c.png)\n\n   \n\nClearly, this is a circle of radius $3$ centered at $(1,2).$ But how can we determine the center and radius from the given circle equation?\n\nLet's start with the equation\n\n$$\nx^2 +  y^2 - 2x - 4y = 4.\n$$\n\nBy grouping the $x$ and $y$ terms and completing the squares, we can write the equation in the standard form\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nWe carry out the process with the following steps:\n\n**Step 1. **Group the $x$ and $y$ terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2x-4y & =4 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+({y}^{2}-4y) & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2.** In each group, add the square of half the linear coefficient to both sides of the equation. \n\n- Here, the $x$ coefficient is $-2,$ so we add $\\left( \\dfrac{-2}{2} \\right)^2 = (-1)^2 = 1$ to both sides.\n\n- Likewise, the $y$ coefficient is $-4,$ so we add $\\left( \\dfrac{-4}{2} \\right)^2 = (-2)^2 = 4$ to both sides.\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-2x+1)+({y}^{2}-4y+4) & =4+1+4 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x+1)+({y}^{2}-4y+4) & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** Finally, we factor each group into a perfect square, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & ={3}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can see that the equation represents a circle centered at $(1,2)$ with radius $3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079635 #edb/ref 1065 2440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079635 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a8743599-a677-56de-8b27-1b1b04f19643" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079635 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236745 #edb/ref 1080 "center: $(0,-\\frac{1}{2})$, radius: $\\frac{3}{4}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236745 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236745 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "921a2627-ec10-5d1e-8639-eef8fd7f3342" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236813 #edb/ref 1080 "center: $(0,\\frac{1}{4})$, radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236813 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236813 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9fb55b6d-6427-54d7-925a-0d7d4383ae68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236953 #edb/ref 1080 "center: $(0,-\\frac{1}{4})$, radius: $\\frac{3}{4}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236953 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 175921