 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432240 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432240 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432240 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432240 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432234 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432240 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432240 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432240 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186432227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432240 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c017ab2c-4452-50b0-937f-c0713b32da2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432241 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432241 #edb/ref 1069 "q-76372" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432241 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432241 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n${x}^{2}-9x+18=4y-{y}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432241 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "05b6d7d5-d625-5b32-8cf2-e194a924cafa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432241 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-9x+18 & =4y-{y}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-9x)+({y}^{2}-4y) & =-18 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}x+{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & =-18+{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}x+{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & =\\frac{25}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & ={(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(\\frac{9}{2},2)$ and its radius is $\\frac{5}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432242 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432242 #edb/ref 1069 "q-76373" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432242 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432242 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+7=7y-2x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432242 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "11173788-8230-54a4-a1cf-e31575312fe3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432242 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+7 & =7y-2x \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x)+({y}^{2}-7y) & =-7 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}y+{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}) & =-7+{1}^{2}+{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}y+{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}) & =\\frac{25}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x+1)}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{7}{2})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2} \\\\ {(x-(-1))}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{7}{2})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-1,\\frac{7}{2})$ and its radius is $\\frac{5}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432243 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432243 #edb/ref 1069 "q-15464" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432243 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432243 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4y=12.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432243 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1da6dc7e-65e3-5087-87df-4fd7079a93cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432243 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4y & =12 \\\\ {x}^{2}+({y}^{2}+4y) & =12 \\\\ {x}^{2}+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & =12+{2}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-0)^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-0)^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2} & ={4}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(0,-2)$ and its radius is $4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432244 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432237 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432244 #edb/ref 1069 "q-15466" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432244 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432244 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2}=80.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432244 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3d51e7e2-42da-5029-94ba-a383fb96ca48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432244 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2} & =80 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+{y}^{2} & =80 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+{y}^{2} & =80+{1}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+{y}^{2} & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={9}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(1,0)$ and its radius is $9.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432245 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432245 #edb/ref 1069 "q-5182" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432245 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432245 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}-12x+{y}^{2}-16y-21=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432245 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "81e4046d-ee12-5213-9139-6081d308b0b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432245 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-12x+{y}^{2}-16y-21 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-12x+{y}^{2}-16y & =21 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 8y+{8}^{2}) & =21+{6}^{2}+{8}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 8y+{8}^{2}) & =121\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-6)^{2}+(y-8)^{2} & ={11}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(6,8)$ and its radius is $11.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432246 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432236 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432246 #edb/ref 1069 "q-54216" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432246 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432246 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}-4x+{y}^{2}-2y=-4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432246 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f5b1b8a2-d088-51d1-b8fc-6a7c6d262461" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432246 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4x+{y}^{2}-2y & =-4 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4x)+({y}^{2}-2y) & =-4 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot y+{1}^{2}) & =-4+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot y+{1}^{2}) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={1}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,1)$ and its radius is $1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
